            <div xml:id="d582">

                <pb facs="0508" n="496" sameAs="frus:frus1940v05/pg496"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">611.3531/1589: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Tuck</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Buenos
                                Aires</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1940-09-20T13:00:00-03:00">September 20, 1940—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received September 20—11:56 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>428. Department’s 216, September 19, 1 p.m. We presume that the preliminary
                    conversations are to be considered as strictly confidential and will so inform
                    the Foreign Office.</p>
                <pb facs="0509" n="497" xml:id="pg497"/>
                <p>If at a later date, possibly when the text of the corn agreement is received
                    here, the Department should wish to give publicity to the negotiations, it is
                    urged that the Embassy be advised in advance.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Tuck</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
